  "description": "The 2026 election for Minnesota's 5th Congressional District will be held on November 3, 2026, with primary elections scheduled for August 11, 2026. The district encompasses eastern Hennepin County, including Minneapolis and the suburbs of St. Louis Park, Richfield, Crystal, Robbinsdale, Golden Valley, New Hope, and Fridley. Incumbent Democrat Ilhan Omar, first elected in 2018, is seeking re-election and faces a competitive primary challenge from Julie Le and Latonya Reeves, while the Republican primary features Dalia Al-Aqidi (the 2024 nominee), John Nagel, and Angie Windhauser. The seat is rated as Safe Democratic by major nonpartisan forecasters due to the district's strong Democratic lean, but the primary contests reflect ongoing intraparty debate about representation and policy direction.",
